# RFC 1122 4.2.2.13: with no timestamps on the old connection, a SYN in
# TIME_WAIT whose sequence number is beyond RCV.NXT (2 here) is accepted as a
# new connection, as Linux does. The new ISN is at least 65537 past the old
# SND.NXT.
0      listen 8080
+0     < S 0:0(0) win 65535 <mss 1460>
+0     > S. 0:0(0) ack 1 <mss 1460>
+0.005 < . 1:1(0) ack 1 win 65535
+0     accept

+0.010 close
+0     > F. 1:1(0) ack 1
+0.005 < . 1:1(0) ack 2 win 65535
+0.005 < F. 1:1(0) ack 2 win 65535
+0     > . 2:2(0) ack 2
+0     state TIME_WAIT

+1     expect_new_isn 65539
+0     < S 3:3(0) win 65535 <mss 1460>
+0     > S. 0:0(0) ack 4 <mss 1460>
+0     state CLOSED
+0.005 < . 4:4(0) ack 1 win 65535
+0     accept
+0     state ESTABLISHED
